-- Sample data for the Larga prototype demo. Places are real Naga locations; coops, plates and drivers are made up.
-- Fares follow LTFRB (jeepneys, from Sept 28, 2026) and Naga City Ord. 2024-002 (tricycles). Not official data.
--
-- How to run: open the Supabase SQL Editor, paste this whole file and run it ONCE, after migration 2
-- (20261026180527_add_modern_jeepney) is pushed. It is safe to run twice: every row has a fixed id and
-- "on conflict do nothing", so a second run adds nothing.
-- The last statement lists the coop ids you need to promote accounts (see the comment above it).
--
-- Terminal and route data come from data/routes/*.json (Matt's files). GeoJSON is [lng, lat]; the columns are lat and lng.
-- Destination coordinates are the last point of each route line. route_line is the LineString geometry only.
-- Fares: traditional jeep PHP 14 for the first 4 km + PHP 2 per km after; modern jeep PHP 17 + PHP 2.40 per km after
-- (straight per km on the route line length, rounded to 0.1 km; no partial-km rule is in the repo). Discounted = 20% off, 2 decimals.
-- Every jeep route has two rows: 'jeepney' (traditional) and 'modern_jeepney'.

